    dummy(a, b, c, d, e, chksum);  // function call
}
```
The variable `j` is written in iteration nl but not read again in iteration nl+1 within the loop body (only used at line 16 after the loop). The global arrays are passed to `dummy()`, but without its definition and given typical TSVC benchmark patterns where `dummy()` prevents dead-code elimination without modifying input arrays, there are no observable inter-iteration dependences through the arrays.

